sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant Frontend
    participant API as Core API
    participant DB as Relational Database
    participant Queue as Message Queue
    participant Worker as Timetable Solver Worker
    participant CLI as Timetable Solver

    User->>Frontend: Request timetable generation
    Frontend->>API: POST /solver/jobs with preferences
    API->>DB: Load scheduling domain data
    DB-->>API: Events, venues, modules, and access data
    API->>API: Build and validate SolverInput
    API->>DB: Create queued solverJob
    API->>Queue: Enqueue timetable.solve job
    API-->>Frontend: 202 Accepted with jobId

    Queue-->>Worker: Deliver solve job
    Worker->>API: GET /solver/jobs/:jobId/input
    API->>DB: Read canonical SolverInput
    DB-->>API: SolverInput
    API-->>Worker: 200 OK with input JSON
    Worker->>CLI: Solve timetable with requested engine
    CLI-->>Worker: Feasible SolverResult
    Worker->>API: POST /solver/jobs/:jobId/callback
    API->>DB: Persist result and completed status
    API-->>Worker: 202 Accepted

    loop Until solver job completes
        Frontend->>API: GET /solver/jobs/:jobId
        API->>DB: Read solverJob status
        DB-->>API: Completed status
        API-->>Frontend: Job status and result metadata
    end
    Frontend->>API: GET /solver/jobs/:jobId/result
    API->>DB: Read solver result
    DB-->>API: SolverResult
    API-->>Frontend: 200 OK
    Frontend-->>User: Display generated timetable
